Lois, do I need to do anything
tomorrow that doesn't involve...

15:29.478 --> 15:32.682
me being bent over in excruciating
pain 3 feet from a toilet?

15:32.858 --> 15:36.523
LOIS: No.
- Time for some tikka masala.

15:39.364 --> 15:42.899
Doctor, I won't lie to you.
I'm a little uncertain about this.

15:43.077 --> 15:44.951
That's perfectly natural, Mrs. Griffin.

15:45.121 --> 15:48.572
And you should ask as many questions
as you can before you decide.

15:48.749 --> 15:52.370
So how does it work, doc? You go
hacking at her like Sweeney Todd?

15:52.547 --> 15:57.505
No, no. Good Lord! This is not 2005.
We've come a long way since then.

15:57.678 --> 15:59.718
So you go stabbing in there
with a laser...

15:59.889 --> 16:04.052
and you try to zap it out like burning
an ant with a magnifying glass?

16:04.226 --> 16:06.055
- No, Mr. Griffin.
- What? So, what?

16:06.228 --> 16:08.851
You hold her legs open
and send a pit bull in there?

16:09.024 --> 16:11.101
You know, one of them
little rat hunting dogs?

16:11.277 --> 16:13.518
And he comes back out with it
in his mouth and he goes:

16:13.695 --> 16:14.727
[GROWLING]

16:14.905 --> 16:17.741
And you can't get it away from him
because, you know, it's his thing.

16:17.909 --> 16:22.204
No. Mr. Griffin, it's a very simple, safe
procedure in which we very precisely...

16:22.373 --> 16:25.741
and delicately remove the embryo.
We do it all the time.

16:25.918 --> 16:28.491
And I promise, it's virtually risk free.

16:28.671 --> 16:31.542
Well, I have to say
I feel a little better about it.

16:31.716 --> 16:34.089
I think this may be
the right thing to do.

16:34.261 --> 16:36.882
Mrs. Griffin,
we have a saying around here:

16:37.055 --> 16:41.054
- Let's keep abortion safe, legal, and rare.
- Okay. Well, why don't you get started?

16:41.227 --> 16:45.142
I'm gonna go sit in the car and pretend
like I'm driving. I'm gonna be in a race.

16:45.899 --> 16:47.773
[PEOPLE SHOUTING INDISTINCTLY]

16:50.112 --> 16:52.070
Hey, what are you guys
bellyaching about?

16:52.240 --> 16:54.945
Sir, we are doing all that we can
to stop the killing...

16:55.118 --> 16:58.154
of millions of unborn babies.
If you have a few moments...

16:58.330 --> 17:00.323
I'd like you to watch
this video presentation.

17:00.499 --> 17:03.335
Yeah, I got a few minutes.
My wife's getting an abortion.

17:07.841 --> 17:11.459
Hello, friend. I hear you're
contemplating having an abortion.

17:11.636 --> 17:14.174
But before you do, remember,
science has proven...

17:14.347 --> 17:17.967
that within hours of conception,
a fetus has started a college fund...

17:18.144 --> 17:22.012
and has already made your first
Mother's Day card out of macaroni.

17:24.653 --> 17:26.062
Aw!

17:26.236 --> 17:29.239
But don't take my word for it.
Just ask my little friend Ziggy.

17:29.408 --> 17:31.945
Hi! I'm Ziggy the Zygote.

17:32.118 --> 17:35.819
I'm looking forward to being
an active member of your community.

17:35.998 --> 17:37.375
Can I hug you?

17:37.543 --> 17:39.534
Ha-ha-ha. Of course you can, Ziggy.

17:39.710 --> 17:43.295
Because even though they're not
visible yet, you already have tiny arms.

17:43.466 --> 17:47.214
Arms that will one day work,
play, and fold in prayer.

17:47.387 --> 17:50.720
- Yay!
- But uh-oh, what's this?

17:50.891 --> 17:52.717
[SCREAMS]

17:52.892 --> 17:54.351
Oh, my God!

17:54.519 --> 17:58.102
Well, he's gone, just like so many
other promising human lives...

17:58.274 --> 18:00.433
who were probably snuffed out
by abortion.

18:00.610 --> 18:02.851
Like the guy
who would have killed Hitler.

18:03.028 --> 18:04.987
Nice going, Schweinhund!

18:05.156 --> 18:06.817
<i>The fourth Stooge. That's right.</i>

18:06.993 --> 18:09.069
<i>There were supposed
to be four Stooges.</i>

18:09.245 --> 18:11.570
It was gonna be hilarious!

18:11.748 --> 18:15.496
<i>And Osama bin Laden's
America-Ioving older brother.</i>

18:15.668 --> 18:17.661
I would have talked him out of it!

18:17.838 --> 18:21.538
Wow, thanks a lot for 9/11,
abortion enthusiasts.

18:21.716 --> 18:23.876
And remember,
not only is abortion murder...

18:24.053 --> 18:27.671
but it's also larceny, jaywalking,
and securities fraud.

18:27.849 --> 18:29.509
Did you know the baby you abort...

18:29.684 --> 18:32.556
may also have a baby inside of it
that you're aborting?

18:32.730 --> 18:35.351
Now that you know this,
do you want an abortion?

18:35.524 --> 18:37.730
No! No, I do not!

18:41.239 --> 18:44.741
Peter, what the hell are you doing?
Have you lost your mind?

18:44.911 --> 18:48.909
Don't you worry, unborn fetus child.
I am here to save you and protect you.

18:49.082 --> 18:50.577
I have seen the light!

18:50.751 --> 18:53.586
Bless you, sir.
You should be very proud of yourself.

18:53.753 --> 18:56.423
Oh, I am. Prouder than
when I was a peacock.

18:56.590 --> 18:59.163
Griffin, nice work
on the Anderson account.

19:16.488 --> 19:18.030
So how did it go at the clinic?

19:18.197 --> 19:20.868
Fine at first,
but then there was a complication.

19:21.036 --> 19:23.739
- We have decided against the procedure.
- Really? Why?

19:23.912 --> 19:25.658
Because it's killing babies, Brian.

19:25.833 --> 19:28.998
If God wanted us to kill babies,
he'd make them all Chinese girls.

19:29.169 --> 19:31.328
Peter, it's not a baby.
It's a fertilized egg.

19:31.505 --> 19:34.044
- It's the size of a pin tip.
- It's alive, isn't it?

19:34.217 --> 19:36.375
To kill any living thing is an abortion.

19:36.552 --> 19:40.302
The man outside the clinic told me.
And he had a t-shirt on that confirmed it.

19:40.474 --> 19:41.802
Okay. Well, sperm is alive.

19:41.975 --> 19:44.467
And every time you masturbate,
millions of them die.

19:44.646 --> 19:46.305
So is it wrong to kill sperm?

19:46.481 --> 19:48.141
Yes. Yes, it is.

19:48.316 --> 19:50.309
No more masturbating in this house.

19:50.485 --> 19:52.064
- What?
- Why?

19:52.239 --> 19:53.897
Because masturbation is abortion.

19:54.072 --> 19:56.694
But abortion helps me
get my homework done...

19:56.869 --> 19:59.239
and sometimes I abort in my sleep.

19:59.411 --> 20:01.321
What am I supposed to do about that?

20:01.499 --> 20:03.455
Peter, I'm sorry
if you disagree with me.

20:03.625 --> 20:06.496
But according to the law,
it is still my right to choose...

20:06.670 --> 20:09.457
what I do with my body.
- Well, the law is wrong, Lois!

20:09.633 --> 20:12.835
Okay, Peter, if you're so pro-life,
let me ask you this.

20:13.011 --> 20:16.132
Would you go down to the orphanage
and claim an unwanted baby...

20:16.308 --> 20:18.880
and take care of it?
- I'm here to save the unborn.

20:19.060 --> 20:21.551
Once out of the vagina,
they can go fuck themselves.

20:21.730 --> 20:24.517
What's inside Lois won't be
remotely human for six months.

20:24.691 --> 20:27.313
There's no brain activity
until at least the 27th week.

20:27.486 --> 20:31.104
It's still a person. It's a woman's
responsibility to carry it to term.

20:31.281 --> 20:32.563
Well, what if a woman is raped?

20:32.743 --> 20:35.068
Should've thought
before she asked me for directions.

20:35.246 --> 20:37.118
- Huh?
- What about incest, Peter?

20:37.289 --> 20:39.198
- What's incest?
- You know how Cousin Lou...

20:39.374 --> 20:41.284
has that kid whose eyes touch?

20:41.461 --> 20:43.583
You're saying Touch Eyes
doesn't deserve to exist?

20:43.754 --> 20:45.831
You don't mind him
when you want a needle threaded.

20:46.008 --> 20:49.423
- They should have had the option.
- How can you say that?

20:49.594 --> 20:52.429
Think of all the love he's given
to Uncle Mom and Aunt Dad?

20:52.597 --> 20:55.171
Okay, this isn't working.
What if carrying the baby to term...

20:55.352 --> 20:56.847
would endanger the mother's life?

20:57.020 --> 20:58.764
I don't know seven of those words.

20:58.939 --> 21:03.648
What if you see that the baby's gonna
be born with no arms and no legs?

21:03.819 --> 21:05.065
You name it Mat.

21:05.238 --> 21:06.269
[HONKING]

21:06.446 --> 21:08.654
Peter, I honestly don't care
what you say.

21:08.826 --> 21:11.696
I am going back to that clinic
and I'm having that abortion.

21:11.870 --> 21:13.862
- Oh, no, you're not!
- Oh, yes, I am!

21:14.038 --> 21:15.368
Now, you get out of my way.

21:15.541 --> 21:17.368
You go and I'll blow the place up!

21:17.543 --> 21:19.999
<i>- You wouldn't.
- You've seen Family Guy. I would.</i>

21:20.171 --> 21:22.498
So, what,
you'd kill a bunch of doctors...

21:22.675 --> 21:25.878
to show them that killing is wrong?
Does that make sense to you, Peter?

21:26.053 --> 21:27.797
- Well...
- Does it?

21:27.972 --> 21:29.348
I...

21:29.515 --> 21:32.884
guess not.
- So, what the hell do we do, huh?

21:33.060 --> 21:34.722
I mean,
we're not gonna solve anything...

21:34.897 --> 21:37.387
by standing here
screaming at each other.

21:37.566 --> 21:39.689
You and I are in this together, Peter.

21:39.861 --> 21:44.238
And whatever we decide, we both have
to agree that it's the right thing to do.

21:44.407 --> 21:45.570
Well, so now what?

21:45.742 --> 21:48.530
I say we go upstairs
and have a long talk.

21:48.704 --> 21:50.862
And we don't come down
until we've made a decision...

21:51.040 --> 21:52.284
that we both can live with.

21:52.457 --> 21:53.491
[SIGHS]

21:53.669 --> 21:54.949
All right, Lois.

22:01.428 --> 22:03.586
Well, I think we made
the right decision.

22:03.763 --> 22:06.385
I mean, sure, having a baby
costs a fortune.

22:06.558 --> 22:08.385
There's cutbacks on things we love.

22:08.560 --> 22:12.429
There's diapers, and crying,
and late nights with no sleep.

22:12.607 --> 22:16.356
Flu shots, and mumps,
and driver's ed, and college tuition.

22:16.528 --> 22:17.808
But you know what?

22:17.987 --> 22:20.444
It's one more person
to share the world with.

22:20.616 --> 22:23.486
Another little voice
in the back seat of the car.

22:23.660 --> 22:26.994
One more Griffin to love
and to love us in return.

22:29.000 --> 22:30.198
We had the abortion.

22:30.199 --> 23:31.199
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru